# ads.txt — Authorized Digital Sellers
#
# DO NOT upload an invented ads.txt. A wrong or empty ads.txt can make ad
# networks refuse to serve ads on your domain.
#
# WHEN TO ADD THIS FILE
# After you register with an ad network, that network gives you a line to
# paste here. Copy it exactly as they show it, then save this file as
# "ads.txt" (no .example) in the site root and redeploy.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHAT THE LINES LOOK LIKE (examples only — do NOT copy these, they are
# other people's identifiers and would not authorize your site)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Google AdSense:
#   google.com, pub-0000000000000000, DIRECT, f08c47fec0942fa0
#
# Monetag:
#   monetag.com, <your-publisher-id>, DIRECT
#
# Adsterra:
#   adsterra.com, <your-publisher-id>, DIRECT
#
# PropellerAds:
#   propellerads.com, <your-publisher-id>, DIRECT
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# RULES
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. One line per authorized seller. Format: <domain>, <publisher id>, DIRECT
# 2. Never add a network you have not signed up with.
# 3. If you have no accounts yet, it is better to have NO ads.txt at all
#    than a file full of placeholders.
# 4. After the site is live, check it at https://yourdomain.com/ads.txt
#    and at https://adstxt.guru to confirm it is readable.
#
# Once you have a real line to add, either paste it into "ads.txt" in the
# site folder, or run:
#   node setup.js --ads "google.com, pub-1234567890, DIRECT, f08c47fec0942fa0"
